-- title:
--   Local 4×4 matrix frame transporting τ, j and the order R
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and rationals $c,d$ such that $H'=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,c,d]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt c d r`: $c<0$, $d<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the completion $H'\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division ring (every nonzero element is a unit) exactly when $r$ lies in $v$. Let $O$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $H'$ that is a maximal order, i.e. $O$ contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $H'$ over $\mathbb Q$, is finitely generated, and every order containing it equals it. Let $j:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\to M_2(H')$ and $\tau:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(H')$ be $\mathbb Q$-algebra maps with $\tau$ injective and $\tau(x)j(m)=j(m)\tau(x)$ for all $x,m$, and let $R$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ consisting precisely of those $x$ all of whose matrix entries $\tau(x)_{il}$ lie in $O$. Let $w$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ with $r\notin w$. Then there exist ring homomorphisms $\tau_w:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w\to M_{(\mathrm{Fin}\,2\times\mathrm{Fin}\,2)}(\mathbb Q_w)$ and $j_w:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w\to M_{(\mathrm{Fin}\,2\times\mathrm{Fin}\,2)}(\mathbb Q_w)$ (matrices indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2\times\mathrm{Fin}\,2$) such that $\tau_w(1\otimes c')=c'\cdot 1$ and $j_w(1\otimes c')=c'\cdot 1$ for every $c'\in\mathbb Q_w$; $\tau_w$ is injective; $\tau_w(x)j_w(y)=j_w(y)\tau_w(x)$ for all $x,y$; whenever all entries of $j(m)$ lie in $O$ and $c'$ is a $w$-adic integer, all entries of $j_w(m\otimes c')$ are $w$-adic integers; and for every $x$ in $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$, membership of $x$ in [`Submodule.localBox R w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40), the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes c'$ with $z\in R$ and $c'$ a $w$-adic integer, holds if and only if every entry $\tau_w(x)_{IJ}$ is a $w$-adic integer.
--
--   At a place $w$ where the definite quaternion algebra $H'$ splits, a matrix frame $H'\otimes\mathbb Q_w\cong M_2(\mathbb Q_w)$ carrying the maximal order $O$ to $M_2(\mathbb Z_w)$ is combined with the two commuting embeddings into $M_2(H')$, producing $4\times4$ matrix realisations over $\mathbb Q_w$ in which the local box of the centraliser order $R$ becomes the integral matrices. It is used in the comparison of local boxes for orders arising as centralisers, in the statements on units preserving such boxes and on equality of local boxes away from the ramified place.
